---
description: Controllers and views read current_user, not Current.user
alwaysApply: true
---

# current_user helper

`Authentication` exposes `current_user` as a `helper_method`. Controllers and views call that. Do not reach into `Current.user` from a controller, view, or helper.

```erb
<%# bad %>
<%= Current.user.name %>

<%# good %>
<%= current_user.name %>
```

```ruby
# bad
Current.user.organizations.find(params[:organization_id])

# good
current_user.organizations.find(params[:organization_id])
```

`current_user` is the one place that may read `Current.user`.
